---
id: field-groups
title: Build Reusable React Form Sections with Field Groups
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related fields often travel together. A scheduling form might need start and end\ntimes, consistent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HH:mm"},{"type":"text","value":" formatting, and a rule that prevents the end from\npreceding the start. Another form needs the same behavior, but stores those\nvalues at different paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A field group makes that component reusable by defining it around the fields it\nneeds rather than the shape of a particular parent form. Each form can then bind\nits own field paths to the component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide assumes you are comfortable creating fields with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":". See the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Quick Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for that foundation. If you only need to\nmove fields from one known form into another file, start with\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../../splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"a-section-tied-to-one-form","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A section tied to one form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suppose an availability editor stores its times at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"availability.opensAt"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"availability.closesAt"},{"type":"text","value":". A natural first step is to extract those inputs into a\ncomponent that accepts the editor's concrete form type. We can even put the\nblur formatter in that component so its caller does not have to repeat it."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { AvailabilityForm } from './form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime } from './time-utils'\n\nfunction AvailabilityTimeRange({ form }: { form: AvailabilityForm }) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>Availability</legend>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.opensAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Opens at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.closesAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Closes at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx\"","title":"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx","file":"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-1","data-tab-index":"1"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { formOptions, type ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const availabilityFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    availability: {\n      opensAt: '',\n      closesAt: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport type AvailabilityForm = ReactFormType<typeof availabilityFormOptions>","lang":"ts","meta":"file=\"form.ts\"","title":"form.ts","file":"form.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-2","data-tab-index":"2"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"TextInput.tsx\"","title":"TextInput.tsx","file":"TextInput.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-3","data-tab-index":"3"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"file=\"time-utils.ts\"","title":"time-utils.ts","file":"time-utils.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx\"},{\"slug\":\"file-1\",\"name\":\"form.ts\"},{\"slug\":\"file-2\",\"name\":\"TextInput.tsx\"},{\"slug\":\"file-3\",\"name\":\"time-utils.ts\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx\",\"code\":\"import type { AvailabilityForm } from './form'\\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\\nimport { formatTime } from './time-utils'\\n\\nfunction AvailabilityTimeRange({ form }: { form: AvailabilityForm }) {\\n  return (\\n    <fieldset>\\n      <legend>Availability</legend>\\n      <form.Field\\n        name=\\\"availability.opensAt\\\"\\n        listeners={[\\n          {\\n            triggers: ['blur'],\\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\\n          },\\n        ]}\\n      >\\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\\\"Opens at\\\" />}\\n      </form.Field>\\n      <form.Field\\n        name=\\\"availability.closesAt\\\"\\n        listeners={[\\n          {\\n            triggers: ['blur'],\\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\\n          },\\n        ]}\\n      >\\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\\\"Closes at\\\" />}\\n      </form.Field>\\n    </fieldset>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"},{\"title\":\"form.ts\",\"code\":\"import { formOptions, type ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\nexport const availabilityFormOptions = formOptions({\\n  defaultValues: {\\n    availability: {\\n      opensAt: '',\\n      closesAt: '',\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\nexport type AvailabilityForm = ReactFormType<typeof availabilityFormOptions>\",\"language\":\"ts\"},{\"title\":\"TextInput.tsx\",\"code\":\"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\nexport function TextInput({\\n  field,\\n  label,\\n}: {\\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\\n  label: string\\n}) {\\n  return (\\n    <label>\\n      {label}\\n      <input\\n        name={field.name}\\n        value={field.value}\\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\\n      />\\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\\n        <small key={error.message} role=\\\"alert\\\">\\n          {error.message}\\n        </small>\\n      ))}\\n    </label>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"},{\"title\":\"time-utils.ts\",\"code\":\"export function formatTime(value: string) {\\n  const match = /^(\\\\d{1,2}):(\\\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\\n  if (!match) return value\\n\\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\\n\\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a useful component for the availability editor. It owns the input\nwiring and turns a value such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:5"},{"type":"text","value":" into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"09:05"},{"type":"text","value":" when the field loses focus.\nThe limitation appears when a booking form stores the same concept at\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schedule.departureTime"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schedule.arrivalTime"},{"type":"text","value":". Both the form type and\nthe field names tie this component to the availability form."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We could type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form"},{"type":"text","value":" as a union of every form that uses the time range,\nbut that makes the API difficult to use. It also means constantly fixing\nits type as more forms need it. The time range does not care which form owns the\nvalues, it only needs certain fields with the declared value types."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"define-virtual-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define virtual fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's turn that dependency around. We have fields that need a certain type and depend on each other.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" lets us define the contract that we expect any given form to complete. Since the fields can come from\nanywhere, the field group can give them virtual names. This time range will call them "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned definition connects that contract to a React component in two\nsteps. Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields"},{"type":"text","value":" value types the field group API that can be used within the component, while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bindComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncreates a callable wrapper that a form can render."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup((helper) => ({\n  // Both virtual fields must bind to concrete fields typed exactly as string.\n  // To only allow the exact type, use `strict`.\n  start: helper.strict<string>(),\n  end: helper.strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields(_props: {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  // ...\n  return null\n}\n\nexport const TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  TimeRangeFields,\n  // The prop that receives the field-group API.\n  'fields',\n)","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"","title":"TimeRangeSection.tsx","file":"TimeRangeSection.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup((helper) => ({\\n  // Both virtual fields must bind to concrete fields typed exactly as string.\\n  // To only allow the exact type, use `strict`.\\n  start: helper.strict<string>(),\\n  end: helper.strict<string>(),\\n}))\\n\\nfunction TimeRangeFields(_props: {\\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\\n  label: string\\n}) {\\n  // ...\\n  return null\\n}\\n\\nexport const TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\\n  TimeRangeFields,\\n  // The prop that receives the field-group API.\\n  'fields',\\n)\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parent form still owns the field values and their default state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We will fill in the component body in the next section. For now, its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields"},{"type":"text","value":"\nprop is limited to the declared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" paths, including their field\ncomponents, methods, and values."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Why `bindComponent`?","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The selected prop keeps its name, but its role changes. Inside the component,\nit contains the field-group API. At the call site, it contains the\nvirtual-to-concrete field map.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bindComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" covers both the runtime as well as the types for you."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-field-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add field behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now we can implement formatting and validation against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":". The\nblur listeners normalize both values, while the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" validator watches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand reports an error when the end precedes it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the example, enter "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:5"},{"type":"text","value":" in either field, then move focus away. The value\nbecomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"09:05"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"time-range-field-group-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"time-range-field-group","data-collapsed-indexes":"[1,2,3]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/App.tsx\",\"environment\":\"react\",\"files\":{\"/App.tsx\":\"import { defineFieldGroup, useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\\nimport { formatTime, toMinutes } from './time-utils'\\n\\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\\n  start: strict<string>(),\\n  end: strict<string>(),\\n}))\\n\\ninterface TimeRangeFieldsProps {\\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\\n  label: string\\n}\\n\\nfunction TimeRangeFields({ fields, label }: TimeRangeFieldsProps) {\\n  return (\\n    <fieldset>\\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\\n      <fields.Field\\n        name=\\\"start\\\"\\n        listeners={[\\n          {\\n            triggers: ['blur'],\\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('start', formatTime),\\n          },\\n        ]}\\n      >\\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\\\"Start time\\\" />}\\n      </fields.Field>\\n      <fields.Field\\n        name=\\\"end\\\"\\n        validators={[\\n          {\\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\\n            watchFields: ['start'],\\n            run: ({ value }) => {\\n              const start = toMinutes(fields.getFieldValue('start'))\\n              const end = toMinutes(value)\\n\\n              if (start !== undefined && end !== undefined && end < start) {\\n                return 'End time must not be before the start time'\\n              }\\n            },\\n          },\\n        ]}\\n        listeners={[\\n          {\\n            triggers: ['blur'],\\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('end', formatTime),\\n          },\\n        ]}\\n      >\\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\\\"End time\\\" />}\\n      </fields.Field>\\n    </fieldset>\\n  )\\n}\\n\\nconst TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(TimeRangeFields, 'fields')\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const form = useForm({\\n    defaultValues: {\\n      availability: {\\n        opensAt: '',\\n        closesAt: '',\\n      },\\n      schedule: {\\n        departureTime: '08:30',\\n        arrivalTime: '10:00',\\n      },\\n    },\\n  })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main>\\n      <TimeRangeSection\\n        form={form}\\n        label=\\\"Availability\\\"\\n        fields={{\\n          start: 'availability.opensAt',\\n          end: 'availability.closesAt',\\n        }}\\n      />\\n      <TimeRangeSection\\n        form={form}\\n        label=\\\"Travel schedule\\\"\\n        fields={{\\n          start: 'schedule.departureTime',\\n          end: 'schedule.arrivalTime',\\n        }}\\n      />\\n      <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => state.values}>\\n        {(values) => (\\n          <pre aria-label=\\\"Form values\\\">{JSON.stringify(values, null, 2)}</pre>\\n        )}\\n      </form.Subscribe>\\n    </main>\\n  )\\n}\",\"/package.json\":\"{\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@tanstack/react-form\\\": \\\"2.0.0-alpha.2\\\",\\n    \\\"react\\\": \\\"19.2.3\\\",\\n    \\\"react-dom\\\": \\\"19.2.3\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\"/TextInput.tsx\":\"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\nexport function TextInput({\\n  field,\\n  label,\\n}: {\\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\\n  label: string\\n}) {\\n  return (\\n    <label>\\n      {label}\\n      <input\\n        name={field.name}\\n        value={field.value}\\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\\n      />\\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\\n        <small key={error.message} role=\\\"alert\\\">\\n          {error.message}\\n        </small>\\n      ))}\\n    </label>\\n  )\\n}\",\"/time-utils.ts\":\"export function formatTime(value: string) {\\n  const match = /^(\\\\d{1,2}):(\\\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\\n  if (!match) return value\\n\\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\\n\\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\\n}\\n\\nexport function toMinutes(value: string) {\\n  const match = /^([01]\\\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\\\d)$/.exec(value)\\n  if (!match) return undefined\\n  return Number(match[1]) * 60 + Number(match[2])\\n}\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineFieldGroup, useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime, toMinutes } from './time-utils'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface TimeRangeFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields({ fields, label }: TimeRangeFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"start\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('start', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"end\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            watchFields: ['start'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const start = toMinutes(fields.getFieldValue('start'))\n              const end = toMinutes(value)\n\n              if (start !== undefined && end !== undefined && end < start) {\n                return 'End time must not be before the start time'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('end', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nconst TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(TimeRangeFields, 'fields')\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      availability: {\n        opensAt: '',\n        closesAt: '',\n      },\n      schedule: {\n        departureTime: '08:30',\n        arrivalTime: '10:00',\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Availability\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'availability.opensAt',\n          end: 'availability.closesAt',\n        }}\n      />\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Travel schedule\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'schedule.departureTime',\n          end: 'schedule.arrivalTime',\n        }}\n      />\n      <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => state.values}>\n        {(values) => (\n          <pre aria-label=\"Form values\">{JSON.stringify(values, null, 2)}</pre>\n        )}\n      </form.Subscribe>\n    </main>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=time-range-field-group env=react file=/App.tsx entry","title":"/App.tsx","file":"/App.tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=time-range-field-group file=/TextInput.tsx collapsed","title":"/TextInput.tsx","file":"/TextInput.tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"export function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}\n\nexport function toMinutes(value: string) {\n  const match = /^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\d)$/.exec(value)\n  if (!match) return undefined\n  return Number(match[1]) * 60 + Number(match[2])\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"group=time-range-field-group file=/time-utils.ts collapsed","title":"/time-utils.ts","file":"/time-utils.ts"},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@tanstack/react-form\": \"2.0.0-alpha.2\",\n    \"react\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.2.3\"\n  }\n}","lang":"json","meta":"group=time-range-field-group file=/package.json collapsed","title":"/package.json","file":"/package.json"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both time ranges apply the same formatting and validation even though their\nvalues use different paths in the parent form."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"bind-the-group-to-a-form","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bind the group to a form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields"},{"type":"text","value":" prop maps each virtual field to a concrete path. TypeScript checks\nthat every mapping exists and that each destination satisfies its field slot."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form applies the current map to field rendering, field methods,\nvalidators, listeners, and their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":". When the end validator watches\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":", it therefore resolves the start path for the same time-range instance."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Dynamic paths are allowed","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bindings may include array indices and other runtime paths, such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ranges[${index}].start"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The field group remains part of the parent form. It uses the parent's state,\nvalidation lifecycle, and submission. It does not create a nested form or a\nseparate submit boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"read-field-group-values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read field-group values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The range validator reads the current start time with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields.getFieldValue('start')"},{"type":"text","value":". That is a good fit for a value needed only\nwhile an event is running."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When rendered output should react to several group values, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields.atom"},{"type":"text","value":"\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":". The selector stays typed to the virtual fields and does not\nsubscribe the component to unrelated form values."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\ninterface TimeRangeSummaryProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeSummary({ fields }: TimeRangeSummaryProps) {\n  const start = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.start)\n  const end = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.end)\n\n  return (\n    <output>\n      {start} to {end}\n    </output>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"","title":"TimeRangeSection.tsx","file":"TimeRangeSection.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\ninterface TimeRangeSummaryProps {\\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\\n}\\n\\nfunction TimeRangeSummary({ fields }: TimeRangeSummaryProps) {\\n  const start = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.start)\\n  const end = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.end)\\n\\n  return (\\n    <output>\\n      {start} to {end}\\n    </output>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" remains useful for parent form metadata such as submission\nattempts or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSubmitting"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"warning","title":"Avoid parent form values","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent form values can have any shape. Read values through the field-group\nAPI instead. Form metadata remains safe to access."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"omit-identity-mappings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omit identity mappings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This binding map adds no information when the parent form already stores\ncompatible fields at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"<TimeRangeSection\n  form={form}\n  label=\"Office hours\"\n  fields={{\n    start: 'start',\n    end: 'end',\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"OfficeHoursForm.tsx\"","title":"OfficeHoursForm.tsx","file":"OfficeHoursForm.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"OfficeHoursForm.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"OfficeHoursForm.tsx\",\"code\":\"<TimeRangeSection\\n  form={form}\\n  label=\\\"Office hours\\\"\\n  fields={{\\n    start: 'start',\\n    end: 'end',\\n  }}\\n/>\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this case, omit the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fields"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. Supply it only to reroute virtual names,\nand include every virtual field when you do."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"choose-strict-or-loose-bindings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose strict or loose bindings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The time-range group uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict<string>()"},{"type":"text","value":" because its formatter and inputs\nexpect ordinary strings. Strict slots accept only concrete fields with exactly\nthe declared value type. This catches a surprising binding before the section\ncan read or write it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loose<T>()"},{"type":"text","value":" when the concrete field type may be narrower than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concrete field type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict<number | null>()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loose<number | null>()"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✓"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✓"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✓"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✓"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | null | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage-in-form-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage in Form Composition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":" can define its own field components, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" does not know of them ahead of time.\nIf you want to use field components in field groups, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineAppFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. The remaining syntax is exactly the same."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFormHook } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\n\nconst { defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextInput,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst appTimeRangeGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction AppTimeRangeFields({\n  fields,\n  label,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof appTimeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field name=\"start\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"end\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const AppTimeRangeSection = appTimeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  AppTimeRangeFields,\n  'fields',\n)","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx\"","title":"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx","file":"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-1","data-tab-index":"1"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"file=\"TextInput.tsx\"","title":"TextInput.tsx","file":"TextInput.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx\"},{\"slug\":\"file-1\",\"name\":\"TextInput.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFormHook } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\\n\\nconst { defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\\n  fieldComponents: {\\n    TextInput,\\n  },\\n  formComponents: {},\\n})\\n\\nconst appTimeRangeGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\\n  start: strict<string>(),\\n  end: strict<string>(),\\n}))\\n\\nfunction AppTimeRangeFields({\\n  fields,\\n  label,\\n}: {\\n  fields: typeof appTimeRangeGroup.fields\\n  label: string\\n}) {\\n  return (\\n    <fieldset>\\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\\n      <fields.Field name=\\\"start\\\">\\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\\\"Start time\\\" />}\\n      </fields.Field>\\n      <fields.Field name=\\\"end\\\">\\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\\\"End time\\\" />}\\n      </fields.Field>\\n    </fieldset>\\n  )\\n}\\n\\nexport const AppTimeRangeSection = appTimeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\\n  AppTimeRangeFields,\\n  'fields',\\n)\",\"language\":\"tsx\"},{\"title\":\"TextInput.tsx\",\"code\":\"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\\n\\nexport function TextInput({\\n  field,\\n  label,\\n}: {\\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\\n  label: string\\n}) {\\n  return (\\n    <label>\\n      {label}\\n      <input\\n        name={field.name}\\n        value={field.value}\\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\\n      />\\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\\n        <small key={error.message} role=\\\"alert\\\">\\n          {error.message}\\n        </small>\\n      ))}\\n    </label>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}}],"headings":[{"id":"a-section-tied-to-one-form","text":"A section tied to one form","level":2},{"id":"define-virtual-fields","text":"Define virtual fields","level":2},{"id":"add-field-behavior","text":"Add field behavior","level":2},{"id":"bind-the-group-to-a-form","text":"Bind the group to a form","level":2},{"id":"read-field-group-values","text":"Read field-group values","level":3},{"id":"omit-identity-mappings","text":"Omit identity mappings","level":3},{"id":"choose-strict-or-loose-bindings","text":"Choose strict or loose bindings","level":3},{"id":"usage-in-form-composition","text":"Usage in Form Composition","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nRelated fields often travel together. A scheduling form might need start and end\ntimes, consistent `HH:mm` formatting, and a rule that prevents the end from\npreceding the start. Another form needs the same behavior, but stores those\nvalues at different paths.\n\nA field group makes that component reusable by defining it around the fields it\nneeds rather than the shape of a particular parent form. Each form can then bind\nits own field paths to the component.\n\nThis guide assumes you are comfortable creating fields with `useForm`. See the\n[React Quick Start](../quick-start) for that foundation. If you only need to\nmove fields from one known form into another file, start with\n[Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\n## A section tied to one form\n\nSuppose an availability editor stores its times at `availability.opensAt` and\n`availability.closesAt`. A natural first step is to extract those inputs into a\ncomponent that accepts the editor's concrete form type. We can even put the\nblur formatter in that component so its caller does not have to repeat it.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx\"\nimport type { AvailabilityForm } from './form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime } from './time-utils'\n\nfunction AvailabilityTimeRange({ form }: { form: AvailabilityForm }) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>Availability</legend>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.opensAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Opens at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.closesAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Closes at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts file=\"form.ts\"\nimport { formOptions, type ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const availabilityFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    availability: {\n      opensAt: '',\n      closesAt: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport type AvailabilityForm = ReactFormType<typeof availabilityFormOptions>\n```\n\n```tsx file=\"TextInput.tsx\"\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts file=\"time-utils.ts\"\nexport function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThis is a useful component for the availability editor. It owns the input\nwiring and turns a value such as `9:5` into `09:05` when the field loses focus.\nThe limitation appears when a booking form stores the same concept at\n`schedule.departureTime` and `schedule.arrivalTime`. Both the form type and\nthe field names tie this component to the availability form.\n\nWe could type `form` as a union of every form that uses the time range,\nbut that makes the API difficult to use. It also means constantly fixing\nits type as more forms need it. The time range does not care which form owns the\nvalues, it only needs certain fields with the declared value types.\n\n## Define virtual fields\n\nLet's turn that dependency around. We have fields that need a certain type and depend on each other.\n`defineFieldGroup` lets us define the contract that we expect any given form to complete. Since the fields can come from\nanywhere, the field group can give them virtual names. This time range will call them `start` and `end`.\n\nThe returned definition connects that contract to a React component in two\nsteps. Its `fields` value types the field group API that can be used within the component, while `bindComponent`\ncreates a callable wrapper that a form can render.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup((helper) => ({\n  // Both virtual fields must bind to concrete fields typed exactly as string.\n  // To only allow the exact type, use `strict`.\n  start: helper.strict<string>(),\n  end: helper.strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields(_props: {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  // ...\n  return null\n}\n\nexport const TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  TimeRangeFields,\n  // The prop that receives the field-group API.\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe parent form still owns the field values and their default state.\n\nWe will fill in the component body in the next section. For now, its `fields`\nprop is limited to the declared `start` and `end` paths, including their field\ncomponents, methods, and values.\n\n> [!TIP] Why `bindComponent`?\n> The selected prop keeps its name, but its role changes. Inside the component,\n> it contains the field-group API. At the call site, it contains the\n> virtual-to-concrete field map.\n> `bindComponent` covers both the runtime as well as the types for you.\n\n## Add field behavior\n\nNow we can implement formatting and validation against `start` and `end`. The\nblur listeners normalize both values, while the `end` validator watches `start`\nand reports an error when the end precedes it.\n\nRun the example, enter `9:5` in either field, then move focus away. The value\nbecomes `09:05`.\n\n```tsx group=time-range-field-group env=react file=/App.tsx entry\nimport { defineFieldGroup, useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime, toMinutes } from './time-utils'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface TimeRangeFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields({ fields, label }: TimeRangeFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"start\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('start', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"end\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            watchFields: ['start'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const start = toMinutes(fields.getFieldValue('start'))\n              const end = toMinutes(value)\n\n              if (start !== undefined && end !== undefined && end < start) {\n                return 'End time must not be before the start time'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('end', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nconst TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(TimeRangeFields, 'fields')\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      availability: {\n        opensAt: '',\n        closesAt: '',\n      },\n      schedule: {\n        departureTime: '08:30',\n        arrivalTime: '10:00',\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Availability\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'availability.opensAt',\n          end: 'availability.closesAt',\n        }}\n      />\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Travel schedule\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'schedule.departureTime',\n          end: 'schedule.arrivalTime',\n        }}\n      />\n      <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => state.values}>\n        {(values) => (\n          <pre aria-label=\"Form values\">{JSON.stringify(values, null, 2)}</pre>\n        )}\n      </form.Subscribe>\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx group=time-range-field-group file=/TextInput.tsx collapsed\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=time-range-field-group file=/time-utils.ts collapsed\nexport function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}\n\nexport function toMinutes(value: string) {\n  const match = /^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\d)$/.exec(value)\n  if (!match) return undefined\n  return Number(match[1]) * 60 + Number(match[2])\n}\n```\n\n```json group=time-range-field-group file=/package.json collapsed\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@tanstack/react-form\": \"2.0.0-alpha.2\",\n    \"react\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.2.3\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBoth time ranges apply the same formatting and validation even though their\nvalues use different paths in the parent form.\n\n## Bind the group to a form\n\nThe `fields` prop maps each virtual field to a concrete path. TypeScript checks\nthat every mapping exists and that each destination satisfies its field slot.\n\nTanStack Form applies the current map to field rendering, field methods,\nvalidators, listeners, and their `watchFields`. When the end validator watches\n`start`, it therefore resolves the start path for the same time-range instance.\n\n> [!NOTE] Dynamic paths are allowed\n> Bindings may include array indices and other runtime paths, such as\n> `ranges[${index}].start`.\n\nThe field group remains part of the parent form. It uses the parent's state,\nvalidation lifecycle, and submission. It does not create a nested form or a\nseparate submit boundary.\n\n### Read field-group values\n\nThe range validator reads the current start time with\n`fields.getFieldValue('start')`. That is a good fit for a value needed only\nwhile an event is running.\n\nWhen rendered output should react to several group values, pass `fields.atom`\nto `useSelector`. The selector stays typed to the virtual fields and does not\nsubscribe the component to unrelated form values.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\ninterface TimeRangeSummaryProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeSummary({ fields }: TimeRangeSummaryProps) {\n  const start = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.start)\n  const end = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.end)\n\n  return (\n    <output>\n      {start} to {end}\n    </output>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n`fields.Subscribe` remains useful for parent form metadata such as submission\nattempts or `isSubmitting`.\n\n> [!WARNING] Avoid parent form values\n> Parent form values can have any shape. Read values through the field-group\n> API instead. Form metadata remains safe to access.\n\n### Omit identity mappings\n\nThis binding map adds no information when the parent form already stores\ncompatible fields at `start` and `end`.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"OfficeHoursForm.tsx\"\n<TimeRangeSection\n  form={form}\n  label=\"Office hours\"\n  fields={{\n    start: 'start',\n    end: 'end',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIn this case, omit the `fields` prop. Supply it only to reroute virtual names,\nand include every virtual field when you do.\n\n### Choose strict or loose bindings\n\nThe time-range group uses `strict<string>()` because its formatter and inputs\nexpect ordinary strings. Strict slots accept only concrete fields with exactly\nthe declared value type. This catches a surprising binding before the section\ncan read or write it.\n\nUse `loose<T>()` when the concrete field type may be narrower than `T`.\n\n| Concrete field type           | `strict<number \\| null>()` | `loose<number \\| null>()` |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `number \\| null`              | ✓                          | ✓                         |\n| `number`                      | X                          | ✓                         |\n| `null`                        | X                          | ✓                         |\n| `string \\| null`              | X                          | X                         |\n| `number \\| null \\| undefined` | X                          | X                         |\n\n## Usage in Form Composition\n\nSince each `createFormHook` can define its own field components, `defineFieldGroup` does not know of them ahead of time.\nIf you want to use field components in field groups, use `defineAppFieldGroup` instead. The remaining syntax is exactly the same.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { createFormHook } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\n\nconst { defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextInput,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst appTimeRangeGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction AppTimeRangeFields({\n  fields,\n  label,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof appTimeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field name=\"start\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"end\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const AppTimeRangeSection = appTimeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  AppTimeRangeFields,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\n```tsx file=\"TextInput.tsx\"\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: field-groups\ntitle: Build Reusable React Form Sections with Field Groups\n---\n\nRelated fields often travel together. A scheduling form might need start and end\ntimes, consistent `HH:mm` formatting, and a rule that prevents the end from\npreceding the start. Another form needs the same behavior, but stores those\nvalues at different paths.\n\nA field group makes that component reusable by defining it around the fields it\nneeds rather than the shape of a particular parent form. Each form can then bind\nits own field paths to the component.\n\nThis guide assumes you are comfortable creating fields with `useForm`. See the\n[React Quick Start](../quick-start) for that foundation. If you only need to\nmove fields from one known form into another file, start with\n[Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\n## A section tied to one form\n\nSuppose an availability editor stores its times at `availability.opensAt` and\n`availability.closesAt`. A natural first step is to extract those inputs into a\ncomponent that accepts the editor's concrete form type. We can even put the\nblur formatter in that component so its caller does not have to repeat it.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"AvailabilityTimeRange.tsx\"\nimport type { AvailabilityForm } from './form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime } from './time-utils'\n\nfunction AvailabilityTimeRange({ form }: { form: AvailabilityForm }) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>Availability</legend>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.opensAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Opens at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"availability.closesAt\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: ({ fieldApi }) => fieldApi.handleChange(formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Closes at\" />}\n      </form.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts file=\"form.ts\"\nimport { formOptions, type ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const availabilityFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    availability: {\n      opensAt: '',\n      closesAt: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport type AvailabilityForm = ReactFormType<typeof availabilityFormOptions>\n```\n\n```tsx file=\"TextInput.tsx\"\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts file=\"time-utils.ts\"\nexport function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThis is a useful component for the availability editor. It owns the input\nwiring and turns a value such as `9:5` into `09:05` when the field loses focus.\nThe limitation appears when a booking form stores the same concept at\n`schedule.departureTime` and `schedule.arrivalTime`. Both the form type and\nthe field names tie this component to the availability form.\n\nWe could type `form` as a union of every form that uses the time range,\nbut that makes the API difficult to use. It also means constantly fixing\nits type as more forms need it. The time range does not care which form owns the\nvalues, it only needs certain fields with the declared value types.\n\n## Define virtual fields\n\nLet's turn that dependency around. We have fields that need a certain type and depend on each other.\n`defineFieldGroup` lets us define the contract that we expect any given form to complete. Since the fields can come from\nanywhere, the field group can give them virtual names. This time range will call them `start` and `end`.\n\nThe returned definition connects that contract to a React component in two\nsteps. Its `fields` value types the field group API that can be used within the component, while `bindComponent`\ncreates a callable wrapper that a form can render.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup((helper) => ({\n  // Both virtual fields must bind to concrete fields typed exactly as string.\n  // To only allow the exact type, use `strict`.\n  start: helper.strict<string>(),\n  end: helper.strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields(_props: {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  // ...\n  return null\n}\n\nexport const TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  TimeRangeFields,\n  // The prop that receives the field-group API.\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe parent form still owns the field values and their default state.\n\nWe will fill in the component body in the next section. For now, its `fields`\nprop is limited to the declared `start` and `end` paths, including their field\ncomponents, methods, and values.\n\n> [!TIP] Why `bindComponent`?\n> The selected prop keeps its name, but its role changes. Inside the component,\n> it contains the field-group API. At the call site, it contains the\n> virtual-to-concrete field map.\n> `bindComponent` covers both the runtime as well as the types for you.\n\n## Add field behavior\n\nNow we can implement formatting and validation against `start` and `end`. The\nblur listeners normalize both values, while the `end` validator watches `start`\nand reports an error when the end precedes it.\n\nRun the example, enter `9:5` in either field, then move focus away. The value\nbecomes `09:05`.\n\n```tsx group=time-range-field-group env=react file=/App.tsx entry\nimport { defineFieldGroup, useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\nimport { formatTime, toMinutes } from './time-utils'\n\nconst timeRangeGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface TimeRangeFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeFields({ fields, label }: TimeRangeFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"start\"\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('start', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"end\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            watchFields: ['start'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const start = toMinutes(fields.getFieldValue('start'))\n              const end = toMinutes(value)\n\n              if (start !== undefined && end !== undefined && end < start) {\n                return 'End time must not be before the start time'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n        listeners={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['blur'],\n            run: () => fields.setFieldValue('end', formatTime),\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => <TextInput field={field} label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nconst TimeRangeSection = timeRangeGroup.bindComponent(TimeRangeFields, 'fields')\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      availability: {\n        opensAt: '',\n        closesAt: '',\n      },\n      schedule: {\n        departureTime: '08:30',\n        arrivalTime: '10:00',\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Availability\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'availability.opensAt',\n          end: 'availability.closesAt',\n        }}\n      />\n      <TimeRangeSection\n        form={form}\n        label=\"Travel schedule\"\n        fields={{\n          start: 'schedule.departureTime',\n          end: 'schedule.arrivalTime',\n        }}\n      />\n      <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => state.values}>\n        {(values) => (\n          <pre aria-label=\"Form values\">{JSON.stringify(values, null, 2)}</pre>\n        )}\n      </form.Subscribe>\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx group=time-range-field-group file=/TextInput.tsx collapsed\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=time-range-field-group file=/time-utils.ts collapsed\nexport function formatTime(value: string) {\n  const match = /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})$/.exec(value.trim())\n  if (!match) return value\n\n  const hours = Number(match[1])\n  const minutes = Number(match[2])\n  if (hours > 23 || minutes > 59) return value\n\n  return `${String(hours).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}`\n}\n\nexport function toMinutes(value: string) {\n  const match = /^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\d)$/.exec(value)\n  if (!match) return undefined\n  return Number(match[1]) * 60 + Number(match[2])\n}\n```\n\n```json group=time-range-field-group file=/package.json collapsed\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@tanstack/react-form\": \"2.0.0-alpha.2\",\n    \"react\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.2.3\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBoth time ranges apply the same formatting and validation even though their\nvalues use different paths in the parent form.\n\n## Bind the group to a form\n\nThe `fields` prop maps each virtual field to a concrete path. TypeScript checks\nthat every mapping exists and that each destination satisfies its field slot.\n\nTanStack Form applies the current map to field rendering, field methods,\nvalidators, listeners, and their `watchFields`. When the end validator watches\n`start`, it therefore resolves the start path for the same time-range instance.\n\n> [!NOTE] Dynamic paths are allowed\n> Bindings may include array indices and other runtime paths, such as\n> `ranges[${index}].start`.\n\nThe field group remains part of the parent form. It uses the parent's state,\nvalidation lifecycle, and submission. It does not create a nested form or a\nseparate submit boundary.\n\n### Read field-group values\n\nThe range validator reads the current start time with\n`fields.getFieldValue('start')`. That is a good fit for a value needed only\nwhile an event is running.\n\nWhen rendered output should react to several group values, pass `fields.atom`\nto `useSelector`. The selector stays typed to the virtual fields and does not\nsubscribe the component to unrelated form values.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"TimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\ninterface TimeRangeSummaryProps {\n  fields: typeof timeRangeGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction TimeRangeSummary({ fields }: TimeRangeSummaryProps) {\n  const start = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.start)\n  const end = useSelector(fields.atom, (state) => state.end)\n\n  return (\n    <output>\n      {start} to {end}\n    </output>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n`fields.Subscribe` remains useful for parent form metadata such as submission\nattempts or `isSubmitting`.\n\n> [!WARNING] Avoid parent form values\n> Parent form values can have any shape. Read values through the field-group\n> API instead. Form metadata remains safe to access.\n\n### Omit identity mappings\n\nThis binding map adds no information when the parent form already stores\ncompatible fields at `start` and `end`.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"OfficeHoursForm.tsx\"\n<TimeRangeSection\n  form={form}\n  label=\"Office hours\"\n  fields={{\n    start: 'start',\n    end: 'end',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIn this case, omit the `fields` prop. Supply it only to reroute virtual names,\nand include every virtual field when you do.\n\n### Choose strict or loose bindings\n\nThe time-range group uses `strict<string>()` because its formatter and inputs\nexpect ordinary strings. Strict slots accept only concrete fields with exactly\nthe declared value type. This catches a surprising binding before the section\ncan read or write it.\n\nUse `loose<T>()` when the concrete field type may be narrower than `T`.\n\n| Concrete field type           | `strict<number \\| null>()` | `loose<number \\| null>()` |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `number \\| null`              | ✓                          | ✓                         |\n| `number`                      | X                          | ✓                         |\n| `null`                        | X                          | ✓                         |\n| `string \\| null`              | X                          | X                         |\n| `number \\| null \\| undefined` | X                          | X                         |\n\n## Usage in Form Composition\n\nSince each `createFormHook` can define its own field components, `defineFieldGroup` does not know of them ahead of time.\nIf you want to use field components in field groups, use `defineAppFieldGroup` instead. The remaining syntax is exactly the same.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx file=\"AppTimeRangeSection.tsx\"\nimport { createFormHook } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { TextInput } from './TextInput'\n\nconst { defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextInput,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst appTimeRangeGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  start: strict<string>(),\n  end: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction AppTimeRangeFields({\n  fields,\n  label,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof appTimeRangeGroup.fields\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>{label}</legend>\n      <fields.Field name=\"start\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"Start time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"end\">\n        {(field) => <field.TextInput label=\"End time\" />}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </fieldset>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const AppTimeRangeSection = appTimeRangeGroup.bindComponent(\n  AppTimeRangeFields,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\n```tsx file=\"TextInput.tsx\"\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function TextInput({\n  field,\n  label,\n}: {\n  field: FieldWithValue<string>\n  label: string\n}) {\n  return (\n    <label>\n      {label}\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n        aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <small key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </small>\n      ))}\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n"}
